This function works by concatenating the two input strings and then iterating through the combined string. It maintains a balance counter which is incremented for every '(' and decremented for every ')'. If at any point the balance becomes negative, it means there are more closing parentheses than opening ones up to that point, indicating an unbalanced string, so it returns 'No'. At the end of the iteration, if the balance is zero, it means all parentheses are balanced, so it returns 'Yes'. Otherwise, if the balance is not zero, it means the combined string is unbalanced, so it returns 'No'.

